#: ../../../citing.md:1
msgid "Citing PyGMT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../citing.md:3
msgid ""
"If you used PyGMT in your research please consider citing PyGMT. You can "
"either cite the [PyGMT paper](https://doi.org/10.1029/2026GC013105) or the "
"[Zenodo archive](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3781524) of the PyGMT "
"software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../citing.md:7
msgid ""
"It is also strongly recommended to cite the [GMT 6 paper](https://doi."
"org/10.1029/2019GC008515) (which PyGMT wraps around). Note that some modules "
"like `dimfilter`, `surface`, and `x2sys` also have their dedicated "
"citations. Further information for all these can be found at <https://www."
"generic-mapping-tools.org/cite>."
msgstr ""

